  "description": "Octal D flip-flop with three-state outputs. On the rising edge of the shared clock (CP), each Q latches its D. /OE gates only the output buffers: when /OE is low the Q pins present the stored bits; when /OE is high they are Hi-Z (Z). The storage itself is independent of /OE, so a value latched while the outputs are disabled reappears when /OE goes low again.",
